    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion! There is a `repeat_jump` mapping, which is by default `;`. So you can, for example, type `Fx` to search backwards for `x` and then repeat backward jump with `;`. Then possibly jump forward with `f` and repeat forward jump again with `;`. The same goes with `t` and `T`. Is this good enough for you?\r\n\r\nAt the moment I like current design better for its simplicity: `f` and `t` always jump forward, `F` and `T` always jump backward, `;` always repeats previous jump.",
